{-
   Two bare `main`s (J91).

   # resolver: ownership
   # target: bare

   A bare entry may have any arity, so both of these are candidates, and before J91 whichever came
   first in the file was the entry - swapping the two lines changed the program. The loader enters
   one function and there is no call site to select at, so more than one `main` is refused by name,
   as the shipping stage refuses a duplicate.
-}

fn main(magic: U32) -> U32 = magic

fn main(magic: U32, info: Size) -> U32 = magic
